{
  "requirement": "The SDK presents node inputs using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\nIts text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet contents = domain.node_content(&node_id)?;\nlet text = contents.format();\n```\n\nLoading and fallible preparation occur in `Domain::node_content` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`. For inputs queued on an ask\nbuilder, these failures return `ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node`\ntool call, they are returned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue\nand recover.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `judge.rendering`.\n\n**1. Inputs are presented through `NodeContents::format`.**\n- `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` swaps in a formatter that returns `formatted input: <contents>`. It asserts that the user message sent to the agent contains `formatted input: source`. This shows a queued input (`contents_of_current_node`) is rendered by the domain's format output, not the raw contents.\n- `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer` checks that multiple inputs are rendered into the message in order.\n- `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` checks that queued inputs reach the agent in order, with repeated nodes preserved.\n- `agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` uses the `distinct_pages` formatter, which adds an `ALPHA-CONTENTS` or `BETA-CONTENTS` label. The `ParallelConversations` provider asserts that the history contains the label, including the last `read_node` page delivered after turn 0. That label exists only in format output, so it shows the `read_node` tool path also uses `format`.\n- `domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement` checks the habeas domain's `format` output on supplied contents.\n\n**2. Text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.**\n- `identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot` changes the underlying contents after the read. It asserts that `format()` still returns \"before\" and that `fingerprint()` still equals the snapshot fingerprint. It also asserts the domain was read only once, so formatting performs no further resource reads.\n- `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` asserts that the recorded dependency fingerprint matches the content that was formatted.\n- `authoring_keeps_the_prepared_subject_snapshot_and_concrete_version` covers the same property for habeas authoring: the original snapshot is kept after the file changes.\n\n**3. Failures.**\n- Ask builder: `queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation` covers read, edge, and prepare failures. A read failure gives `ValidationError::Graph(\"read\")`, an edge failure gives `Graph(\"edges\")`, and a prepare/render failure gives `Graph(\"render\")`. It asserts no dependency is recorded and the agent is not invoked again. `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` adds the missing-agent case.\n- `read_node` tool: `node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents` makes preparation fail. It asserts the next request carries an error tool result for `read_node` with the failure text. It then lets the agent continue and submit, and asserts the `ask` call succeeds with no dependencies recorded.\n\n**Gaps.** None found. `a_complete_node_read_has_text_and_no_continuation` is an unmarked `read_node` success test, but the marked tests above already cover that path, so I did not treat it as a marking gap.",
  "references": "f6ca580b7ad3955509357366e0e56b0d72b32452bd72e328b9bd2bf30481a0de",
